/-!
# Theorem B: the certified lattice duals (explore34)

From the named hypotheses CertB (θ = 4/7, λ = 0.775) and CertB1 (θ = 1, λ = 0.595), the
Arb-checked inequalities of verify_dual.py, Lemma 1 gives: no admissible f has J_θ(f) > 1 for
0 ≤ θ ≤ 4/7, λ ≤ 0.775 (resp. 0 ≤ θ ≤ 1, λ ≤ 0.595). The certificate data and the side
conditions (η_k = -1 for k < k0, η_k ≥ -1) are checked in Lean by decide (kernel).
-/

